cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "turbidity-sensor"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A low-cost turbidity sensor and its software, for monitoring culture density in a running
  bioreactor. It uses the circuit board from a TST-10-type turbidity probe (as sold on DFRobot's
  SEN0189 module), mounted in a 3D-printed case around a clear tube and read by an Arduino Nano.
  A timed syringe actuator draws culture from the vessel through the tube for each reading. The
  repository contains the printed cases, a C library that models and calibrates the sensor, the
  Arduino firmware, the sampler logger, and the bench and bioreactor data.
keywords:
  - turbidity
  - optical density
  - photobioreactor
  - microalgae
  - open hardware
  - arduino
authors:
  - family-names: "Brooks"
    given-names: "Cameron"
version: "0.6.0"
url: "https://github.com/uwo-fast/turbidity-sensor"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uwo-fast/turbidity-sensor"
